   "text": "The SMILES below was read region by region from the drawing.\n\n- **Left heterocycle:** an imidazo[1,2-a]pyrazine carrying a cyclopropyl on the pyrazine carbon, a 1H-pyrazol-4-yl on the imidazole carbon next to the bridgehead nitrogen, and an NH link at C8.\n- **Aryl amide:** the NH connects to a 2-fluoro-4-carbonylphenyl ring, and the carbonyl forms an amide with one nitrogen of a piperazine.\n- **Linker:** the other piperazine nitrogen carries CH2C(=O)NH, followed by a chain of six CH2 groups ending in an aryl ether oxygen.\n- **Right aryl ring:** the oxygen sits on a benzene ring that has a CH2NH group ortho to the oxygen and a 4-methylthiazol-5-yl group para to the CH2.\n- **VHL-type end:** the CH2NH is acylated by a hydroxyproline unit, drawn as the 4-hydroxy-pyrrolidine-2-carboxamide with one wedge and one hash. Its ring nitrogen is acylated by tert-leucine, whose NH carries a 1-fluorocyclopropanecarbonyl group.\n- **Stereochemistry:** I took the three stereocentres from the standard VHL ligand (VH032-type) SMILES, where the hydroxyproline is (2S,4R) and the tert-leucine is (S). I matched this to the drawn wedges and hashes by recall of that standard form, not by working out each centre from the image.\n\nSMILES: O=C(c1ccc(Nc2nc(C3CC3)cn3c(-c4cn[nH]c4)cnc23)c(F)c1)N1CCN(CC(=O)NCCCCCCOc2cc(-c3scnc3C)ccc2CNC(=O)[C@@H]2C[C@@H](O)CN2C(=O)[C@@H](NC(=O)C2(F)CC2)C(C)(C)C)CC1"
  }
